course: dictionary
lesson: 10948
title: Waistcoat: a sleeveless jacket
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A waistcoat is a short jacket with buttons and no sleeves, worn over a shirt. You can work out the meaning from the clues around the word: it has buttons, it has no sleeves, and it goes over a shirt.
explain: «The White Rabbit pulls a watch out of his waistcoat pocket.» A pocket is a clue. A waistcoat has pockets, so it is something small things can be kept in.
explain: «He reaches for his waistcoat pocket and finds no money.» Swap in your meaning to check: a short buttoned jacket with no sleeves, worn over a shirt, fits the sentence and makes sense.
explain: In the UK this garment is called a waistcoat. In the USA and Canada it is called a vest, so an American book may say vest where a British book says waistcoat.
fact: A waistcoat is a short jacket with buttons and no sleeves.
fact: It is worn over a shirt, and often under a suit jacket.
fact: «A three-piece suit» means a jacket, trousers and waistcoat.
fact: Men used to carry pocket watches on a chain, often in a waistcoat pocket.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a waistcoat is called a vest.
exercise: What is a waistcoat? | A pair of trousers with a pocket | A long coat with sleeves that reaches the knees | A hat worn in the rain | *A short jacket with buttons and no sleeves, worn over a shirt
exercise: «He reaches for his waistcoat pocket.» Where would a waistcoat pocket be? | *On a waistcoat, which is worn over a shirt | Inside a school bag | On a shoe | On the sleeve of a coat
exercise: In the USA and Canada, what is a waistcoat called? | A jumper | A cardigan | *A vest | A blazer
test: Which word is the American name for a waistcoat? | Blazer | Jacket | Shirt | *Vest
test: In a three-piece suit, which piece is the waistcoat? | *The sleeveless, buttoned piece worn over the shirt and under the jacket | Trousers | A tie | The jacket with long sleeves
exam: In «The White Rabbit pulls a watch out of his waistcoat pocket», which word is the clue that shows a waistcoat can hold small things? | The word Rabbit | The word pulls | *The word pocket | The word White
